THEORY 11: REQUEST SPAM AS TRIGGER
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Response elaborated:
"CPU stress alone, even on ALL 3 masters, does NOT cause the IO
cascade storms you've been seeing. The host is fine absorbing 80%
CPU load."

"What actually happens during a real cascade:
- Multiple controllers do LIST operations against apiserver
  simultaneously
- Apiserver forwards to etcd
- etcd does fsync on WAL for every write
- 3 etcds fsync to same NVMe
- Disk queue builds
- Everything waiting on disk piles up"

"CPU stress doesn't create LIST storms or fsync spam. That's why
your test didn't cascade."

